  "function_revised": "Membrane protein encoded as the terminal gene of the F1F0-ATP synthase operon (Rv1303-atpBEFGHDC-Rv1312; operon structure established in the published M. tuberculosis oxidative-phosphorylation literature), co-transcribed with the atp genes and under strong purifying selection. The convergent context — co-transcription within the ATP-synthase operon, predicted membrane localisation, and an in-vivo fitness requirement (Tn-seq) — makes it a candidate accessory / associated component of the mycobacterial ATP synthase (oxidative phosphorylation). Whether it is a structural subunit, an assembly factor, or a co-regulated membrane protein is not established. RefSeq leaves it 'hypothetical protein'.",
